// A list of strings is freed with its strings when it holds only strings built
// for it and none was read out where something keeps it. pieces is such a list
// and is fresh, so the caller owns it (and both strings); cut reads a piece into
// an operand only. Freed: the list and 2 strings from each of the 2 calls to
// pieces, which main binds to a name and passes straight to cut.
pieces(string s) {
  string[] xs = [];
  push(xs, s + "1");
  push(xs, s + "2");
} return string[] xs;

cut(string[] ys) {
  int n = len(ys[0]) + len(ys[1]);
} return int n;
